WEBVTT

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.110
It's finally time for the screening...

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:11.050
I wonder how our short turned out.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.110
I'm kinda nervous.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.540
Sorry. I barely managed 
to finish editing in time,

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.290
so none of you got a chance 
to get a look at it.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.500
Don't sweat it.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.080
We've come this far. I'm ready 
to trust you to the end, Kyoya.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.310
Seriously!

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.800
If it wasn't for you, we might 
not've had anything to turn in!

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.290
Yeah! I bet it's gonna be okay!

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.760
Okay, attention!

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:35.410
We're going to start screening the shorts you
produced for the first comprehensive exercise.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:41.020
As you know, this screening 
is an actual part of your course work.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.470
That said, once something's 
become an artistic project...

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.900
It needs to be ready for audience appraisal.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.800
Everyone here is a creator, 
but they're also spectators here

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.930
expecting to see something worthwhile.

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:57.600
If it's funny, go ahead and laugh, 
and you can applaud at the end.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.030
But the opposite also applies.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:04.020
Because your friends made it... 
Because they tried their hardest...

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.640
You can stow all of that pitiful nonsense.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.160
I expect your sincere reactions 
as students in a visual arts program.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.260
<i>In other words, if it's not good, 
there'll be no response.</i>

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.830
<i>The theater will be frozen over, 
and you'll be finished.</i>

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.180
Hashiba...

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:21.970
We're gonna win.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.500
<i>The screenings will now begin.</i>

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:02.950
Completed
Comprehensive
Exercise
 Screening

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.870
That was awesome! I'm touched!

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.000
<i>Kawasegawa's team did an amazing job.</i>

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.600
We're in trouble.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.830
I didn't think anyone 
would have a silent film.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.430
It was amazing even without 
any sound or dialogue.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.970
You could really tell 
how the protagonist felt.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.570
It was real pretty looking, too.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.810
<i>In terms of how much of a refined, 
finalized product it is...</i>

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.790
<i>Their project blows ours out of the water.</i>

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.560
Next is Team Kitayama's short film.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.110
Aw, man...

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.990
Ours takes place at a train station, too...

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:35.250
Folks are gonna compare them, huh?

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.030
<i>We did everything we possibly could. So...</i>

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:40.850
<i>Please!</i>

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.460
A Team Kitayama Film

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.640
Huh? Photos?

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.680
I didn't know using stills was an option.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:07.810
<i>This is...</i>

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:17.420
<i>This was the only thing I could think of 
when we found out about the camera.</i>

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.320
We're going to figure something out, damn it!

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.330
What's gotten into you, Kyoya-kun?

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.240
"Figure something out"?

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.690
Look, I know I'm the one who screwed up...

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.040
But how are we doing anything 
with this equipment?!

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.480
We're supposed to be making a film, 
not taking still pictures!

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:36.790
No. We can do this.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.920
Don't be crazy! Just let it go!

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.130
We'll have to give it another crack 
when the next project...

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:42.130
We can do this.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.100
I know we can. Trust me.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:49.970
I'm going to make sure all 
of your hard work pays off.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:54.850
<i>That's right... I've gotten 
through spots like this already.</i>

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:59.750
<i>I've cooked up a promotional movie 
with next to no assets before.</i>

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:04.990
<i>What did I do? I used After Affex, 
Promiere, Photoshot...</i>

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:07.600
<i>The school should have 
access to all of them.</i>

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:10.280
<i>I'm not letting their efforts be wasted!</i>

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.040
Hey, Kiryu here...

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.960
Hey, it's Hashy! Are you ready 
to join the club?

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.710
All Comers Welcome

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.710
I'll do it! I'll join, so...

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.550
I need you to teach me how 
to take good stills!

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.820
Well? Does it fit with our concept?

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:32.600
Yeah! It oughta work great.

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:37.090
From what Kiryu-san said, 
we're going to need 100 shots per cut.

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:38.660
A hundred?!

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:42.710
Yeah. So we're going to be shooting 
with the camera in a fixed position.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.480
What should I do, then?

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:45.770
You don't need to worry.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.530
Once the clapperboard cues you,
 give it a few seconds,

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.720
and then act it out like you would 
if we were filming things.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.630
Will that work?

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:52.960
It should.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.280
We'll pick the best options available 
from out of the pictures that get taken.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.950
Okay, got it!

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.860
We're gonna be dubbing 
in the dialogue later?

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.100
Right.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:06.080
So, we're going to need to adjust the script 
based on how long the cuts run.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.100
That's cool.

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:11.760
Don't worry so much... 
I'm not gonna pitch a fit again.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.410
Thanks!

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:14.890
Shinoaki...

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:15.600
Yeah?

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:20.730
I want the composition to be the kind of thing 
that only works with still photography.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.070
I know how hard that'll be, but you're 
the only person who can handle it.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:26.620
Are you up to it?

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:29.050
Yeah! I'll try!

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:31.450
I wanna get you what you need!

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:34.210
One last thing, does anyone 
have a digital camera on them?

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.370
I've got one.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:38.620
But the picture quality's pretty bad.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:40.090
That's okay.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.890
<i>All right. This should do it.</i>

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.250
Thanks again, Nanako.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:52.930
<i>The 15 seconds of video we took 
with Nanako's digital camera...</i>

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.480
<b>As
it
ever
was</b>

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:58.480
<b>I
wait
for
you</b>

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.480
<b>as
my
black
 hair</b>

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.480
<b>flutters 
in
the
wind</b>

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:58.480
<b>until the
day the frost
covers the
 ground</b>

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:04.230
<i>We then take the still shots in order 
to put the story together.</i>

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:08.150
<i>We only have three minutes. 
And in that time...</i>

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:44.690
<b>And
as
the
white</b>

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:44.690
<b>of
old
age
mingles</b>

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:44.690
<b>with
my
black
hair,</b>

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.690
<b>I find
that
my
ardor</b>

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:44.690
<b>for you
has grown
no less
brilliant</b>

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:05.070
<i>Was it no good?</i>

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:15.840
Holy crap, Team Kitayama!

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:17.110
No way...

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:19.870
Is it me, or are we getting more applause?

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:21.330
This is great!

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.440
Impressive.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.820
<i>Kawasegawa's team came in first place...</i>

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:39.240
<i>Which was kind of expected.</i>

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:41.990
<i>But we came in third...</i>

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:44.800
<i>That's some fairly high praise.</i>

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:49.770
<i>But if we had been able to film things 
the way we originally intended...</i>

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:51.210
<i>I bet we would've been better received.</i>

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:57.970
Listen... I know you might have some issues 
with how the edit turned out, but—

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.510
This is <i>so</i> damn frustrating!

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:02.480
What the hell, man?!

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:05.590
I had <i>no</i> idea what you were doing 
when we were shooting,

00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:08.580
but it turned into a proper story, 
with a proper ending and everything!

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:11.860
You're really something, man! You did great!

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:14.880
But... if my script...

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:19.740
Not the first one, but the one 
I redid with your input...

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:23.220
If we had been able to use it properly, 
it would've turned out great!

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:27.530
Maybe even better than what we turned in...

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:28.920
Y-Yeah.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.290
I'm bitter, too!

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:32.990
Kyoya, that was seriously amazing!

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:35.660
To be able to come up 
with an idea like that...

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:38.510
I was just doing what I was told,

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:43.020
so I'm kinda... No, I'm seriously impressed!

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:47.490
But... I can act well 
in a normal film too, so...

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:50.310
So I'm sure that'd... y'know...

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.190
Whatever! I'm just gonna say it!

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.490
I know I can put on a really 
good performance!

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:59.240
So I want to get to act the normal way!

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:01.740
Kyoya-kun...

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:05.140
You play kinda dirty, huh?

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.410
You're usually so quiet...

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:12.880
And then you get all fired up, 
with your eyes flashing.

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:16.800
During the shoot... 
And during the screening...

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:19.220
I was full of butterflies the whole time!

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:25.660
Hey, I'm locking up. If you want to 
review things, do it somewhere else.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:26.930
Or...

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:29.880
Are you discussing your next goal?

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:30.850
Yes!

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:31.940
This guy is not...

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:32.900
Kyoya isn't...

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.190
Kyoya-kun ain't...

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.690
...gonna show me up!

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:40.560
Well, that's great to hear.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:44.020
You're going to have another assignment 
waiting after vacation is over.

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:46.490
Let's see if you can get some payback.

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:47.330
Right!

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:49.740
Good answer!

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.210
First, we need to review what went wrong.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:54.710
And let's skip my screw-up 
with the equipment.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:57.000
That is obviously going to 
be the first thing we discuss.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:00.550
I'm gonna keep the runtime and other stuff 
in mind when I do the storyboard next time.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.890
That goes for the script, too.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:05.980
And I'm gonna put on a performance 
that'll blow Kyoya's mind!

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.540
Sounds like fun!

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:15.140
<i>The Platinum Generation that I looked up to, 
and wanted to get close to...</i>

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:19.130
<i>If I've been able to make them 
feel the heat, even a little...</i>

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:25.060
<i>Then this remake of mine 
might be going well, after all.</i>

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.030
I don't buy it!

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:31.610
Why wasn't Hashiba's team given first place?

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:33.580
It's pretty simple, really.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:37.280
What they turned in was a little too 
unorthodox for a school assignment.

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:40.500
Plus, I get the feeling 
it wasn't intentional.

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:43.960
I'd guess they had an issue 
when requisitioning their equipment.

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.520
Are you serious?

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:49.750
That film wasn't completely thought through.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:54.560
That said, I might have 
an interesting bunch in this class.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:58.170
If they really did come up with that footage 
to work around some kind of trouble in production,

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:03.310
it speaks to an incredible amount 
of problem-solving potential in Hashiba Kyoya.

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:04.450
You're right...

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:09.090
Which means that, for the second semester,

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:12.130
I want you working with Hashiba's team.

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:16.830
You're interested in him, aren't you?

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:20.150
Well, I suppose.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:25.930
O-Of course, only in his talent as a producer.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:28.900
Uh, what else would I have meant?

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:32.390
You are the worst sister!

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:35.630
Good grief...

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:41.680
That little sister of mine is adorable, 
no matter how old she gets.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:45.110
<b>Osaka Film
Festival

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:47.590
We're heading home!

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:49.240
Good work today!

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.430
Thanks for coming in today.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:58.100
And sorry you had to cover 
a shift out of the blue.

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:00.480
It's fine. You worked hard too, Nanako.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:02.580
Hey, listen...

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:08.590
Do you have... some free time... today?

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:11.010
Karaoke

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.910
<i>I haven't been to a karaoke 
booth in a long time.</i>

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:19.760
Do you like karaoke?

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:22.120
Yep! I love it.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:25.070
Well, it's more like 
I love music and singing!

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.410
I see.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:33.220
Well, then...

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:39.770
I brushed against 
the freckles that I hated so...

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:41.710
<i>That's impressive volume!</i>

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:42.580
Life goes on and I heave 
a little sigh for you.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.390
<i>And her voice...</i>

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:45.300
It's heavy, the love 
that I once shared with you...

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:46.420
<i>It's like it's resonating in my...</i>

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:48.170
But it dissolved like 
it was just a sugar cube.

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:47.680
<i>Chest?</i>

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:51.090
<i>Wait, is she actually pretty terrible?</i>

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:51.090
Now the little pain sitting in my heart...

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:54.070
Has shrunken a bit, 
but it really does hurt me now.

00:13:54.070 --> 00:13:55.440
Those silly horoscopes...

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:04.280
It feels great to really sing 
after such a long time!

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:07.620
S-Sorry... I'm pretty bad, huh?

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:09.870
Uh, well...

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:15.080
My grandma does traditional 
minyo folk music back home.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.790
And I learned it at a young age, but...

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.380
I'm just no good!

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:24.060
I just can't seem to fix my tone deafness.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:32.100
So I wanted to ask you a favor, Kyoya...

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:33.680
Huh? What is it?

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:36.350
When I'm singing by myself,

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:40.150
I don't really know what 
I need to work on.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:43.740
So, every now and again, 
would you come to karaoke with me...

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:46.970
And listen to my singing?

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:48.350
No?

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.150
Sure, if you'd like my help.

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:54.740
Really?! Awesome!

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:57.000
Thanks, Kyoya!

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:04.880
For some reason, it's really easy 
to sing in front of you!

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.770
That was fun!

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:10.600
By the way, Nanako...

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.300
What's up?

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.530
I just thought of something.

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.390
Once you've practiced, 
and got some confidence,

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:19.480
maybe we can upload your singing online.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:20.880
Online?

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.870
Yeah.

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:25.780
We'll record you singing, 
and put it on a video site.

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.730
A bunch of people will hear you—

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:31.670
No, no, no, no way can I do that!

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:36.560
I'm already crappy enough, 
I don't need to get trashed on top of it!

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:39.060
Th-That's why I said, 
after you get better...

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:41.430
No! Absolutely not!

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:43.250
I mean, the internet is the whole world!

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.800
Can you imagine how embarrassing it is

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:47.340
to go on there practically 
begging for attention?!

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:53.310
Okay, then why don't we do it 
when there's a Japan-only video site?

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.960
Only for Japan?

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.970
Is there such a thing?

00:15:57.970 --> 00:15:59.200
Yeah...

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:02.640
<i>Well, it will be sometime around the end 
of this year or the beginning of next.</i>

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:04.970
What... do you think about that, though?

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.820
I guess that wouldn't be as bad.

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.640
Okay, that settles it!

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:13.690
Let's practice with that as your goal!

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:16.530
Hey! Don't pick my goals for me!

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.250
Sheesh...

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:26.670
Okay, let's celebrate 
the end of the semester,

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:31.370
and the increased budget of the fine arts 
club thanks to our new members.

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:33.350
Cheers!

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:35.440
Cheers!

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:44.630
Let's do the official 
introductions this time.

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:48.270
I'm Kiryu Takashi, in my fifth year 
of the photography program.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.850
Thank you so much for your help, by the way.

00:16:50.850 --> 00:16:52.590
Not a problem!

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:55.360
Especially considering our club 
managed to survive thanks to you!

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:59.830
He's right! Plus, you 
brought us some cute girls.

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:04.400
I'm Hiyama Yurika. I'm in my 
third year of industrial arts.

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:07.610
I sculpt and make stuff like that.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:13.380
Down the hill he fells, the darling acorn!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:19.310
Into the lake he falls, oh me oh my!

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:25.480
I'm Sugimoto Mikio, and I'm in my 
second year of the music program.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:26.980
It's a pleasure.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.900
Despite how he looks, 
he's actually got a lot of skill.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:32.320
Your attention, please!

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:35.300
Allow me to express my joy 
for today... through dance.

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:37.190
A pose to symbolize reception.

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:39.160
One symbolizing hope for the future!

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:42.340
A pose for affection! A pose for courtship!

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:43.310
That's Kakihara Sho. He's in his 
third year of theater arts study.

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:46.540
Note the toes here! See? 
See how they point?!

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:45.600
He's majoring in dance.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:50.660
And now, the Bacchanalia dance!

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:51.880
What we've all been waiting for!

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:54.190
Here it comes! The fine 
arts club specialty...

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:57.130
The eruption of Vesuvius!

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:03.600
It's the tragedy of Pompeii all over again!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:08.600
<b>Higashiyama Bridge</b>

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:08.600
I've got work today, 
so I'll see you two later.

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.900
I'll get dinner ready.

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:12.660
Thanks!

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:19.080
It sure was a lotta fun with 
all our senpai back there, huh?

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:23.330
They're all so eccentric... 
but also really talented.

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:25.310
Kyoya-kun...

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:26.950
What is it?

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:33.040
You know that I draw, don't you?

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.550
You noticed?

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:42.010
I was trying to keep it quiet.

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:46.220
Why didn't I lock the dang door?

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:48.020
I'm sorry for prying—

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:52.180
Aw, don't go apologizing! 
I shoulda been more careful.

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:56.420
Say, do you remember...

00:18:57.770 --> 00:19:03.390
When I said how folks who can't do anything 
are looking for what they can do?

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:04.580
Yeah.

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:09.280
I can't do anything, like the rest of y'all.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:12.320
I'm always messing up, 
even just doing daily stuff.

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:15.420
Bad at school, can't do 
athletic stuff, either...

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:21.370
But there's one thing... 
one thing I like doing.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.700
Making art?

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:28.120
But it just don't seem to come together.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:31.640
I can have fun drawing, 
but can't do much more than that.

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:37.400
I've won some awards, 
but that ain't enough to make a living.

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:40.190
So I thought if I went 
to school for visual arts,

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:43.630
I might get a job in TV or something.

00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:46.000
That's why I enrolled in art school.

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:49.250
But I didn't have the guts 
to try the fine arts program.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:53.670
I'm supposed to like drawing... 
but can't enjoy doing it seriously.

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.230
I have no confidence, either.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:57.590
That's why I was keeping it a secret.

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:04.590
I was hoping one day my eyes 
would light up like yours do.

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:09.770
But it just don't seem to wanna happen.

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.340
No, that's not what I—

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:13.040
So I was thinking...

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:18.980
Maybe I should give up on art. 
Maybe that'd be easier.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:19.730
You can't!

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:24.930
You can't do that! 
You can't stop being an artist!

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:26.780
Kyoya-kun?

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:29.700
I... I...

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:38.860
<i>Your art was always there for me.</i>

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:42.720
I...

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.770
I love your art, Shinoaki.

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:54.330
<i>From all the way in the future...
I've loved it.</i>

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:59.250
You said something during the shoot...

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:03.930
You wanted me to do it... because you thought 
I was the only one who could handle it.

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:06.070
Yeah. I did.

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:10.650
That made me happy. I was real flustered.

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:14.500
I thought, what kinda person 
thinks that about me?

00:21:15.140 --> 00:21:17.420
I'm real curious now.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:25.010
So I've made up my mind! 
Starting now, you're my goal, Kyoya-kun!

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:30.240
I'm gonna study lots, and become 
someone who can create

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:32.350
the kinda worlds you wanna see!

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:35.310
Do you have some kinda goal, too?

00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:38.600
Yeah. I do.

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:41.790
But I can't tell you about it yet.

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.510
Well, that's a real shame.

00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:49.120
But... I'll just have to work hard 
so that you'll tell me someday, huh?

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:52.250
<i>My goal...</i>

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:56.580
<i>One example might be having you say 
those things to me ten years from now.</i>

00:21:57.680 --> 00:22:01.750
<i>The remake of my life... has just begun.</i>
